# Pairs with EpochMeetsCoreOwnAlloc (E -> C). StaleEpochNeverAppends no longer counts an
# epoch below the highest raised one as stale, so a superseded activation appends.
MODULE: EpochMeetsCoreOwnAllocSupersededAppends
TARGET: EpochMeetsCoreOwnAlloc
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a superseded activation's own append is not stale

--- FIND
EStaleUpdate(a) == staleAccepted' = (staleAccepted \/ epoch[a] < maxClaimed \/ epoch[a] <= lRetired)
--- REPLACE
EStaleUpdate(a) == staleAccepted' = (staleAccepted \/ epoch[a] <= lRetired)
--- END
